# steps/named-struct-exec.md §12 (Q45): a `while:` in a named Structure's body is a statement of the body,
# run as in a method's body (before: "a Structure reference field needs a name").  Counter's loop turns
# seven times; executed once from the root, n is 7.  Entry 7.
Counter:
    size_t: n 0U
    size_t: k 0U
    while: k < 7U
        n: n + 1U
        k: k + 1U
return
Counter
size_t: after 9U
after: Counter\n
int: ok 0
if: after = 7U
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
